              <h1 class="display" id="title-sangmo">Sangmo</h1>
              <p class="korean">상모 돌리기</p>
            </header>
            <p class="body">
              <strong>Sangmo-spinning</strong> is one of Korea’s most iconic folk performances, a traditional performing art in which a dancer spins a long ribbon (sangmo) attached to a hat by rotating their head during pungmul (farmers’ music).
              <span class="break"></span>
              Performed to the lively rhythms of nongak, the dancer vigorously whirls the sangmo, showcasing a variety of techniques including circular and spiral patterns.
            </p>
