              <p class="korean">연 날리기</p>
            </header>
            <p class="body">
              <strong>Fly a kite</strong> is one of Korea’s most beloved traditional pastimes, a folk activity in which participants fly elaborately decorated kites during the Lunar New Year and other festive occasions.
              <span class="break"></span>
              Traditional Korean kites, known as bangpae-yeon, feature a distinctive rectangular shape with a circular hole in the center that improves stability in the wind. Flyers often engage in kite-fighting, coating their strings with ground glass to cut opponents’ lines — a thrilling contest of skill, timing, and wind-reading passed down through generations.
            </p>
