              <svg class="corner-mark mark-top" viewBox="0 0 144 144" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#mark-jegi" /></svg>
              <h1 class="display" id="title-jegi">Jaegi-</h1>
              <p class="korean">제기차기</p>
            </header>
            <p class="body">
              Jegi chagi is one of Korea’s beloved traditional games, a folk pastime in which players kick a jegi (a small shuttlecock made from a coin wrapped in paper or cloth) to keep it in the air using their feet.
              <span class="break"></span>
              Played during holidays like Lunar New Year, participants compete to see who can kick the jegi the most times without letting it touch the ground, showcasing balance, agility, and rhythm.
            </p>
            <span class="tally" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <p class="display display-end">Chagi</p>
